#: ../../../source/api/citations.rst:2
msgid "Citations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/citations.rst:4
msgid ""
"Install the optional ``pybamm[cite]`` extra to load and export citations. "
"Downstream packages can load their own BibTeX databases and register "
"citations from their models and parameter sets:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/citations.rst:8
msgid ""
"pybamm.citations.read_citations(\"path/to/CITATIONS.bib\")\n"
"pybamm.citations.register(\"Downstream2026\", reason=\"Downstream model\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/citations.rst:13
msgid ""
"Each citation can be given a reason. Without an explicit reason, the calling "
"class name is used when available. Parameter sets can provide citations as "
"keys or two-string ``(key, reason)`` pairs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/citations.rst:17
msgid ""
"pybamm.ParameterValues(\n"
"    {\"citations\": [\"Chen2020\", (\"Nyman2008\", \"Electrolyte "
"transport\")]}\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/citations.rst:23
msgid "Use ``verbose=True`` to include reasons in the text output:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/citations.rst:25
msgid "pybamm.print_citations(verbose=True)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/citations.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.citations.Citations:1
msgid ""
"Entry point to citations management. This object may be used to record "
"BibTeX citation information and then register that a particular citation is "
"relevant for a particular simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/citations.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.citations.Citations:5
msgid ""
"Citations listed in `pybamm/CITATIONS.bib` can be registered with their "
"citation key. Load other databases with :meth:`read_citations`, or provide a "
"BibTeX citation to :meth:`register`. Requires the optional ``pybamm[cite]`` "
"extra."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/citations.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.citations.Citations:10 pybamm.citations.Citations.print:15
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

